WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.2 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Working out which policies you actually need

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A new initiative needs fewer policies than you think: choose them from what you will do.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.281
A policy states a principle or rule; a procedure explains how people apply it. A new initiative needs fewer policies than you might think, chosen from what you will actually do.

4
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:27.281
Three priority groups

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:38.241
Before you start: A legal duty or a high risk from your very first activity. For example: The youth club needs safeguarding and consent forms before its first pilot session.

6
00:00:38.241 --> 00:00:48.459
Required soon: Triggered by registration, the first hire, growth or a new activity. For example: A contract and HR policies before the bakery’s first paid assistant starts.

7
00:00:48.459 --> 00:01:00.248
Good practice: Useful, but not yet required by law or by your main risks. For example: An environmental policy for the repair café, planned for its second year.

8
00:01:00.648 --> 00:01:01.248
Why fewer is better

9
00:01:01.248 --> 00:01:06.552
1. Copied policies that nobody follows create risks of their own.

10
00:01:06.552 --> 00:01:11.115
2. Focusing on the essentials saves your limited time.

11
00:01:11.115 --> 00:01:17.048
3. Funders and partners can see you know what matters.

12
00:01:17.448 --> 00:01:18.048
What it shapes

13
00:01:18.048 --> 00:01:23.722
1. Your policy register: owner, approval route and review date for each.

14
00:01:23.722 --> 00:01:29.026
2. The core, safeguarding, data and HR policies in this module.

15
00:01:29.026 --> 00:01:34.959
3. Where you need qualified local advice before you launch.

16
00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:35.959
What to avoid

17
00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:40.893
Copying a thick folder of policies from another organisation.

18
00:01:40.893 --> 00:01:46.196
Writing policies without procedures that show how to apply them.

19
00:01:46.196 --> 00:01:52.130
Forgetting what funders and customers will require by contract.

20
00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:54.530
You build a prioritised policy register for your launch and first year.

21
00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:58.530
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:03.130
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
